Z||000000||Heisenhund||05-23-2000||10:57 AM||||I've read with some interest about various recalls on the V6. I looked & found no recall stickers on my vehicle. Then I ran across a picture on one of the websites (the addy escapes me now) of an unrecalled 2.8 and lo and behold I was looking at my engine compartment!!<P>My question is this:<BR>Aside from the various safety improvements concerning engine fires, is there any other advantage to having these recalls completed? The car has 128K on it so warranty isn't a factor (hehhee). Do these mods get me anything tangible? Aside from peace of mind that my little money pit isn't going to burst into flames?<P>Heis<P>P.S.<BR>Had to use my horn the other day. Anybody know of a good replacement that sounds more like an American car than like a wheezy bicycle?<BR>||||reg||5
Z||000001||rogergarrison||05-23-2000||02:57 PM||||there are current recalls for exhaust manifolds with broken bolts/studs, theyll put new manifold on, replace broken ones with new , harder ones, free if it hasnt been done before. another one for free replacement of emergency brake cables on both rear wheels. i know because i just had it all done at the pontiac dealer. cost- $0.00||||reg||1
